      "problem": "Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-(x-1)(x-5).$",
      "worked_solution": "From the equation $y=-(x-1)(x-5),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are $x_1=1$ and $x_2=5.$\n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{x_1+x_2}{2} = \\dfrac{1+5}{2} = 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=3.$",
